{
  "id": "bn-03",
  "kind": "lesson",
  "level": "A1",
  "order": 3,
  "title": "Compound Letters — যুক্তাক্ষর",
  "summary": "How two or more consonants are written as one glyph when no vowel stands between them: the হসন্ত, the common ligatures, য-ফলা, রেফ and র-ফলা, and the special shapes ক্ষ and জ্ঞ.",
