    },
    {
      "id": "ksha-jnya",
      "number": "26",
      "heading": "ক্ষ and জ্ঞ",
      "statement": "Two conjuncts have shapes of their own: ক্ষ is ক + ষ, and জ্ঞ is জ + ঞ. Neither is read by simply saying its parts in order; ক্ষ is often heard as kho, and জ্ঞ in জ্ঞান as gên.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "target": "শিক্ষা",
          "roman": "śikkha",
          "gloss": "education — contains ক্ষ"
        },
        {
          "target": "জ্ঞান",
          "roman": "gên",
          "gloss": "knowledge — contains জ্ঞ"
        }
      ],
      "paradigms": [],
      "footnotes": [
        "Beames already notes ksha pronounced khya and jna pronounced gya."
      ],
      "seeAlso": [
        "conjunct-shapes"
      ],
      "sources": [
